        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6216c9d9-c334-57a7-a5d5-c6167d779199",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Agee, Nelly Sachs, Davis Grubb, Matthew Mead, Ruth Mead, Johannes Bobrowski\n- Works: A Death in the Family, The Night of the Hunter\n- Awards: Pulitzer Prize, Nobel Prize in Literature\n- Roles: film critic, novelist, poet, translator, screenwriter\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1940s, James Agee was one of the most influential film critics in the United States.\n- In 1953, Davis Grubb published the novel The Night of the Hunter.\n- In 1957, James Agee's autobiographical novel A Death in the Family was published.\n- In 1958, James Agee posthumously won the Pulitzer Prize for A Death in the Family.\n- The screenplay for the film The Night of the Hunter was written by James Agee and was based on Davis Grubb's 1953 novel of the same name.\n- In 1966, Nelly Sachs was awarded the Nobel Prize in Literature.\n- Matthew Mead, born in 1924 in Buckinghamshire and died in 2009, was an English poet and, with his wife Ruth, a translator of German poets including Johannes Bobrowski and Nelly Sachs.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
